# One script, every system: Linux (X11), Windows and macOS run it unchanged
# against scriptcheck, which writes down what arrived; run.sh compares that
# with expected.txt.  Coordinates count from the corner of the window's
# inside, and "scale lcl" makes them the same numbers as Left and Top in
# scriptcheckmain.lfm, whatever size the LCL scaled the form to on this
# screen.
#
# What it avoids, because it is not the same everywhere: the End key alone
# (a Mac text field does not move the caret for it), a list item picked by
# where it is drawn (row heights differ), Ctrl+A (a Mac keeps it for "line
# start").  A click past the end of the text and the arrow keys are the
# same on every system.

waitfor 10000 HID Script Check
scale lcl
activate
wait 500
shot 1-start.png

at 150 32
click
type Hello from one script - Grüße é

at 300 76
click
hold shift
key home
let shift
type replaced

at 40 120
click

at 90 160
click
wait 700
click

at 400 30
click
key down
key down
key ctrl+shift+k

at 100 250
click
at 200 260
click r
wait 700
at 300 300
dblclick
wait 700
drag 260 230 420 320
at 150 300
scroll down 3
scroll up 1
wait 300

shot 2-filled.png
at 400 160
click
